window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"drmundo","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Dr. Mundo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Infected Bonesaw is a 4s cooldown against his Q's 10s at rank 1 — you land more than two pokes for each one of his."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Maximum Dosage (120s) answers his execute — cast it before he commits, not after, to stay above the floor."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Ashen Pursuit is a flat 10s blink and auto-reset — the 10s after he spends it is your window."},{"when":"Late","text":"Stacked HP and overheal outrun his execute threshold entirely — you win by continuing to exist."}],"wants":{"you":["Cleaver chip every wave","HP stacking on schedule","Drag the game long"],"foe":["Missing-HP procs on you","Burst windows before items","End before your overheal caps"]},"early":"A patient, even chip war: his Q poke and missing-HP procs genuinely pressure your regen, but your percent-HP cleaver pressures him right back. Trade cleavers for his walk-ups, don't waste health spamming at nothing since the Q costs you HP, and keep the wave near your side so his procs have fewer targets.","mid":"Every stage through first item reads even — his ult threat is answered by Maximum Dosage's overheal, and his AP burst still bites while your regen ramps — so play it steady: chip, farm, stack HP items, and never gift him a low-health window where his execute math works. Time your R before his all-ins, not after.","late":"Two-plus items you simply outgrow him: stacked health and overheal outrun his execute threshold, and he can no longer burst what he can't finish. Walk down the sidelane he can't answer, soak his poke like weather, and cleave him every time he shows — you win by continuing to exist.","whys":["Level 1 is even — his Q poke and missing-HP procs pressure your regen exactly as hard as your cleaver pressures him.","Level 2 stays even skill: no decisive spike for either side, just measured chip and last-hitting.","Level 3 is even — his poke trades roughly balance your percent-HP cleaver, and neither side can force the issue.","Levels 4-5 remain even: his burst still matches your early bulk, so keep trades honest and your health respectable.","Level 6 is even — his ult threat is answered by R Maximum Dosage's overheal. Cast yours before, not after, his commitment.","First item stays even: his AP burst still bites against your ramping regen, so the lane holds its breath one more stage.","Two-plus items are Dr. Mundo's — stacked HP and overheal outrun his execute threshold entirely, and his kill condition dies of old age."]});
