window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"drmundo","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Skill","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"His spike — your cleaver is slow, dodgeable and costs health, and he punishes every whiff with a trade you can't afford."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"A fresh Maximum Dosage erases his kill math mid-fight — hold R for his commit, never as a top-up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your takeover: health stacking plus R regen out-sustains his entire kit, and his trades start losing money."},{"when":"Late","text":"You out-regen his combo, but Aureate Rush scales on your max HP and Determination revives him."}],"wants":{"you":["Cleavers that actually land","Survive levels 2-3","Grievous Wounds before HP"],"foe":["Punish whiffed cleavers","Kill windows before your 6","End the game early"]},"early":"Levels 2-3 are the whole danger zone: your cleaver is slow, dodgeable, and costs health, and he punishes every whiff with a Q-E trade your early frame can't afford. Throw cleavers only at CS-locked moments, farm with basics where safe, and let your passive quietly refill what he chips. It stabilizes at 4-5.","mid":"Level 6 evens the books — his kill pressure is real but a fresh Maximum Dosage erases the math mid-fight, so hold R until he commits, never as a top-up. First item is your takeover: health stacking plus the R regen out-sustains his entire kit, and his burst rotations start losing money on every trade.","late":"You are now the unkillable regen tank his combo simply cannot kill. Shove the sidelane he has to answer, cleave him on cooldown, and take every duel he's foolish enough to offer. In teamfights, walk through his damage to sit on his carries — he can't peel you and he can't race your regen.","whys":["Level 1 opens even — before cooldowns and health costs matter, it's farming and posturing on both sides.","Zaahen takes level 2: your Infected Cleaver is slow, dodgeable, and costs you health he punishes every time it whiffs.","Level 3 stays his — his Q and E out-trade a kit whose only lane tool is that health-draining cleaver. Concede and farm.","Levels 4-5 flatten to even as your farm stabilizes and the approach of Maximum Dosage starts changing his risk math.","Level 6 is even — his kill pressure persists, but a fresh R heal offsets whatever window he thought he had.","First item is Dr. Mundo's: health stacking and R regen out-sustain his burst completely, and his trades start running at a loss.","Two-plus items are yours — an unkillable regen tank his combo simply can't kill. The lane's early tax finally refunds itself."]});
